---
import DocPage from '../layouts/DocPage.astro';
import { stats } from '../data/stats';
import { getPortableWorkflowNames } from '../lib/skillNames';

const adaptedWorkflows = getPortableWorkflowNames().length;
---

<DocPage title="Install" description="Install phxagents v3 for Claude Code, Amp, Codex, Pi, or OpenCode." active="docs">
  <div class="page-head">
        <h1>Install phxagents v{stats.version}</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          One canonical set of <strong>{stats.skills} Elixir &amp; Phoenix skills</strong>, packaged for five AI coding runtimes. Claude Code installs the full plugin with <strong>{stats.agents} named agents and hooks</strong>; Amp, Codex, Pi and OpenCode install generated, runtime-native skill editions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="docs-body">
        <div class="runtime-heading">
          <h2>Choose your runtime</h2>
          <a class="cmd-inline" href="/compatibility/">Compare capabilities →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="runtime-list">
          <a href="#claude-code">
            <span class="runtime-mark">CC</span>
            <span><strong>Claude Code</strong><small>Full canonical plugin · skills, agents, hooks and permissions</small></span>
            <code>/phx:*</code>
          </a>
          <a href="/install/amp/">
            <span class="runtime-mark">A</span>
            <span><strong>Amp</strong><small>Generated Agent Skills · project-local or global</small></span>
            <code>skill: invoke</code>
          </a>
          <a href="/install/codex/">
            <span class="runtime-mark">CX</span>
            <span><strong>Codex</strong><small>Native skills plugin · optional trust-gated safety hook</small></span>
            <code>$elixir-phoenix:*</code>
          </a>
          <a href="/install/pi/">
            <span class="runtime-mark">π</span>
            <span><strong>Pi</strong><small>Native Git skills package</small></span>
            <code>/skill:*</code>
          </a>
          <a href="/install/opencode/">
            <span class="runtime-mark">OC</span>
            <span><strong>OpenCode</strong><small>Generated skills via sparse Git checkout</small></span>
            <code>skill tool</code>
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="callout info">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 11v5"/><path d="M12 8h.01"/></svg>
          <div><strong>Using Amp, Codex, Pi or OpenCode?</strong> Choose it above to open its complete guide. Continue below only to install the full Claude Code plugin.</div>
        </div>

        <h2 id="claude-code">Claude Code — install the full plugin</h2>
        <p>Run these inside Claude Code, one at a time:</p>

        <div class="code-block">
          <div class="code-head">
            <span>1. Add the marketplace</span>
            <button class="copy" data-copy>Copy</button>
          </div>
          <pre>/plugin marketplace add oliver-kriska/claude-elixir-phoenix</pre>
        </div>

        <div class="code-block">
          <div class="code-head">
            <span>2. Install the plugin</span>
            <button class="copy" data-copy>Copy</button>
          </div>
          <pre>/plugin install elixir-phoenix</pre>
        </div>

        <p>A fresh v3 install automatically pulls the small <code>ecto</code> and <code>lv</code> compatibility namespaces that preserve <code>/ecto:*</code> and <code>/lv:*</code> commands. Run <code>/reload-plugins</code> in an open session before using the new skills, agents and hooks.</p>

        <h2>Updating from v2.x</h2>
        <p>Install the new command-compatibility dependencies before updating the main plugin:</p>

        <div class="code-block">
          <div class="code-head">
            <span>Terminal</span>
            <button class="copy" data-copy>Copy</button>
          </div>
          <pre>claude plugin marketplace update oliver-kriska
claude plugin install ecto@oliver-kriska
claude plugin install lv@oliver-kriska
claude plugin update elixir-phoenix@oliver-kriska</pre>
        </div>

        <p>Restart Claude Code afterward. Confirm that <code>/phx:help</code>, <code>/ecto:n1-check</code>, and <code>/lv:assigns</code> appear before continuing work.</p>

        <h2>What gets installed</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Every runtime:</strong> all {stats.skills} canonical skills, complete bundled resources, and {adaptedWorkflows} fully adapted workflows.</li>
          <li><strong>Claude Code:</strong> {stats.agents} specialist agents, lifecycle and enforcement hooks, root instructions, permissions, and full workflow orchestration.</li>
          <li><strong>Amp, Codex, Pi, OpenCode:</strong> generated skill distributions with native names and invocation. Named Claude agents and its broad hook set are not silently emulated.</li>
          <li><strong>Tidewave MCP:</strong> supported when your project and client already expose it; registration remains external to every edition.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>After install</h2>
        <p>In Claude Code, run <code>/phx:intro</code> for a guided walkthrough. In another runtime, load <code>phx-plan</code>, <code>phx-investigate</code>, or <code>phx-review</code> with the native syntax shown in its install guide.</p>

        <div class="code-block">
          <div class="code-head">
            <span>Claude Code</span>
            <button class="copy" data-copy>Copy</button>
          </div>
          <pre>/phx:plan Add a unique constraint on the email column</pre>
        </div>

        <h2 id="security">Security &amp; trust</h2>
        <p>
          The plugin runs skills, agents, and hooks inside Claude Code with your tool
          permissions — so it’s independently scanned with
          <a href="https://github.com/NVIDIA/SkillSpector" rel="noopener">NVIDIA SkillSpector</a>,
          a static security scanner for AI-agent skills. The scan runs with <strong>zero data egress</strong>.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>The baseline-aware repository scan passes</strong> after reviewed false-positive baselines. The current raw totals and every baseline decision live in <a href="https://github.com/oliver-kriska/claude-elixir-phoenix/blob/main/SECURITY.md" rel="noopener">SECURITY.md</a>.</li>
          <li>Lower-scoring <strong>CAUTION</strong> components remain documented rather than being hidden behind baselines.</li>
          <li>The few higher-scoring components are <strong>documented false positives</strong> — a static scanner flags the safety-enforcing and security-auditing skills precisely because they name dangerous patterns in order to <em>forbid or detect</em> them (one flagged line literally reads <code>NEVER bypass security checks for speed</code>).</li>
          <li><strong>No data exfiltration</strong>, <strong>read-only review agents</strong> (source edits disallowed), and <strong>auditable bash hooks</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Read the full report, line-by-line triage, and a reproduce-it-yourself command in
          <a href="https://github.com/oliver-kriska/claude-elixir-phoenix/blob/main/SECURITY.md" rel="noopener">SECURITY.md</a>.
        </p>
  </div>
</DocPage>

<style>
  .page-head h1 {
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.4vw, 38px);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .page-head .lede {
    margin: 0 0 32px;
    color: var(--fg-soft);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 640px;
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .docs-body { max-width: 720px; }
  .docs-body h2 {
    margin: 40px 0 14px;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 20px;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .docs-body h2:first-of-type { padding-top: 0; border-top: 0; margin-top: 0; }
  .docs-body p {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--fg-soft);
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-size: 14.5px;
  }
  .docs-body ul {
    margin: 0 0 16px 0;
    padding-left: 22px;
    color: var(--fg-soft);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .docs-body li { margin: 4px 0; }
  .runtime-heading {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .runtime-heading h2 { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .runtime-heading .cmd-inline {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 36px;
    flex: none;
  }
  .runtime-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 10px;
    margin: 14px 0 22px;
  }
  .runtime-list > a {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 13px 14px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    color: var(--fg-soft);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: border-color 140ms ease, background 140ms ease;
  }
  .runtime-list > a:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--accent-soft);
  }
  .runtime-list > a:first-child { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .runtime-mark {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    color: var(--accent-fg);
    font: 600 10px/1 var(--font-mono);
  }
  .runtime-list > a > span:nth-child(2) {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .runtime-list strong {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .runtime-list small {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .runtime-list code {
    color: var(--accent-fg);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .runtime-heading { align-items: flex-start; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
    .runtime-heading .cmd-inline { min-height: 44px; }
    .runtime-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .runtime-list > a:first-child { grid-column: auto; }
  }
</style>
